module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.AlgebraicClosure
public import WeilConjectures.CategoryTheory.GrothendieckAbelian.Sheaf
public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.EtaleTorsion

/-!
# Finite-stalk subobjects cover a torsion sheaf over a field

Source: the finite stable subgroup argument in blueprint `lem-sc-affine-generic-second`,
paragraph 4; Stacks Project, Tags 04JQ and 03SA.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- Finite-stalk subobjects of a torsion abelian sheaf over a field have supremum top.

Source: blueprint `lem-sc-affine-generic-second`, paragraph 4, finite stable subgroup
construction; Stacks Project, Tag 04JQ (abelian sheaves on a field and discrete Galois
modules) and Tag 03SA (torsion sheaves and constructible approximation).
(blueprint: lem-sc-field-torsion-finite-stalk-subobjects-cover)

Proof: Choose a separable closure inside the algebraic closure. By 04JQ, the geometric
stalk identifies abelian sheaves with discrete continuous modules for the absolute Galois
group. The stalk of M is torsion by the torsion stalk criterion. Each element has an open
stabilizer, so its orbit is finite, since the Galois group is profinite. The subgroup
generated by that orbit is Galois stable and finite: a group generated by finitely many
torsion elements in an abelian group is a quotient of the product of their finite cyclic
groups. Transport its inclusion back through the exact equivalence. Its stalk is the
chosen finite subgroup, and it contains the original element. Thus every element of the
stalk lies in a finite-stalk subobject. The supremum contains all these subobjects, so its
inclusion is surjective on the stalk. It is already monic, hence an isomorphism, since the
stalk over a field is conservative. Therefore the supremum is top. For M = 0 the bottom
subobject already suffices; no finite-generation assumption on M is required. -/
theorem torsion_finite_stalk_subobjects_iSup_eq_top
    (K : Type u) [Field K]
    (M : Sheaf (Spec (.of K)).smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hM : M.IsTorsion) :
    letI : HasColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1}
      (Sheaf (Spec (.of K)).smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
        IsGrothendieckAbelian.hasColimits _
    letI : CompleteLattice (Subobject M) := Subobject.instCompleteLattice.{u + 1}
    let Φ := (pointSmallEtale
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap K (AlgebraicClosure K))))).sheafFiber
        (A := AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (⨆ N : {N : Subobject M // Finite (Φ.obj (N :
        Sheaf (Spec (.of K)).smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}))}, N.val) = ⊤ := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
